==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm}} {{term|gostly|lang=enm}}, {{term|gastlich|lang=enm}}, from {{etyl|ang}} {{term|gastlic|gāstlīċ|spiritual, holy, clerical (not lay), ghastly, ghostly, spectral|lang=ang}}, equivalent to {{suffix|ghost|ly}}. Cognate with {{etyl|sco|-}} {{term|gostly|lang=sco}}, {{term|gastly|lang=sco}}, {{term|gaistlie||spiritual, ghastly, terrifying|lang=sco}}, {{etyl|fy|-}} {{term|geastlik||spiritual, clerical, religious|lang=fy}}, {{etyl|nl|-}} {{term|geestelijk||spiritual, clerical, ecclesiastical|lang=nl}}, {{etyl|de|-}} {{term|geistlich||spiritual, sacred, religious|lang=de}}, {{etyl|da|-}} {{term|geistlig||ecclesiastical, clerical|lang=da}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|en-us-ghostly.ogg|Audio (US)}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|ghostl|ier}}

# Of or pertaining to [[ghost]]s or [[spirituality]].
# [[spooky|Spooky]]; [[frightening]].

